{"note":"Control-station half-breadth offsets measured, like a lines plan, from the approved GameModels3D pasc208 (Hull A) viewing reference in the runtime frame (metres; z bow-negative from midships, y up from the reference waterline). Each row is [z, [[half-breadth, height] ...]] from the keel on the centreline to the deck edge: 19 points from the keel to the waterline, then 7 to the deck edge. Thin appendages (bilge keels, the centre skeg, rudder, shaft struts and bossings, propeller guards) are left out and modelled as fittings; the shell under the outer shaft struts (z 50-66) is the blend of the clean sections either side; the anchor hawse lips and the stem-head fairlead are bridged. The two end rows sit on the hull ends (z = +/-length/2).","length":183.9,"rows":[
